# Ignore everything except what's in package.json "files"
*
!cli.js
!hooks/
!app/
!package.json
!README.md
!LICENSE

# The data directory must never reach the registry: the database holds every
# provider credential in plaintext, and the build home also holds the machine
# id and the jwt secret of the machine that built the package.
#
# Note that npm's "files" field wins over this file, so a rule here cannot
# exclude anything under app/. The real guard is in the build:
# cli/scripts/build-cli.js skips and then purges those directories, and
# tests/unit/cli-build-artifacts.test.js fails the build if one survives.
